!! me-id: amicr038
!   MicroEmacs - Contact Information
!   Contact Information
## CONTACT INFORMATION


  The project is now hosted on Github. For all problems, questions and feature
  requests please use the issue tracker:

    `https://github.com/mittelmark/microemacs/issues`

  The project page is `https://github.com/mittelmark/microemacs` and the release
  downloads are at `https://github.com/mittelmark/microemacs/releases`.

  The historical JASSPA web site `http://www.jasspa.com` still documents the
  releases before 2010 and hosts binaries for old platforms such as DOS,
  Windows 3.1, Solaris and HP-UX.


## Help, FAQ and other queries 

  Before opening an issue please check the [Frequently Asked Questions](Frequently Asked Questions)
  and the project home page, your problem may have already been addressed there.

  From 1997 to 2000 there was a discussion group at egroups.com and from 2001
  to 2010 at yahoogroups. After the final closing of yahoogroups there is no
  news group any more. The old news group content (without attachments) can
  still be retrieved with a Tcl script:
  
  `https://wiki.tcl-lang.org/page/yahoogroups%2Dreader`


## Reporting Problems 

  Open an issue at https://github.com/mittelmark/microemacs/issues and include,
  if possible, the following information:

  __Platform__
 
  >   The host platform, for example `linux`, `darwin`, `cygwin` or `win32`.

  __Version__
 
  >   The version of MicroEmacs. Use `esc-x about` to retrieve the  
     information, the format of the date is `yyyy/mm/dd`, followed by the  
     host system type. e.g.  

            MicroEmacs 09 - Date 2026/10/15 - linux

  __Description__
 
  >  A description of the problem. Try to include as much information as  
     possible. Include any material necessary to reproduce the problem  
     (i.e. macro files, text file that demonstrates problem etc).  


## Suggestions and Feedback 


  Suggestions, new macro templates, themes and other contributions are very
  welcome, please open an issue or a pull request on Github. We appreciate
  macro code fragments for languages that do not yet have a file hook, games,
  color schemes and similar additions.


## Porting 


  If you wish to port MicroEmacs to another platform and are willing to
  undertake responsibility for maintenance of that platform then please let us
  know by opening an issue with the details.
